## Notes & Style

- **`tar.TypeRegA` is deprecated** as of Go 1.13 but still exists. The plan lists it explicitly to handle older tarballs. Keep the constant in the switch case; if the linter complains, it's fine to add `//nolint:staticcheck` as a comment. If Go 1.25 has removed it, fall back to `case tar.TypeReg:`.
- Strict TDD: do not implement before tests are written and shown to fail.
- The helper `buildTarGz` is exported within the test file (lowercase `buildTarGz`, so package-private). Task 5 will reuse it.
- Do NOT add tests for zip-slip / size cap in this task. Task 5 handles those.

## Code Organization

Single file `extract.go` for now. Don't split into `extract.go` + `safepath.go`.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] All 3 tests pass (`TestExtractHappyPath`, `TestExtractEmptyArchive`, `TestExtractMalformedGzip`)
- [ ] `go vet ./...` succeeds
- [ ] `Module.Files` is correctly populated with the expected bodies
- [ ] Empty archive → empty `Files` map (no nil pointer)
- [ ] Malformed gzip → non-nil error
- [ ] Commit message exactly: `feat(birdseye): tar.gz extraction with happy-path coverage`
- [ ] Only `apps/birdseye/internal/archive/` files staged

